circle-pi5-gadget.patch - Circle's DWC2 USB gadget on the Raspberry Pi 5 (BCM2712), on top of circle-gadget.patch
(applied by pi/engine/build.sh with PI5_GADGET=1, and by pi/circle/build-pi5gadget.sh; docs/pi5.md "USB device side").
Written from the Pi 5 device tree (/axi/usb@480000) and Circle's own DWC2 code. GPL-3.0-or-later as Circle.
  - bcm2835.h: ARM_USB_BASE 0x1000480000 on RASPPI 5 (the core, host, device and power offsets as on the Pi 4)
  - bcm2711int.h: ARM_IRQ_USB = GIC SPI 73 on RASPPI 5 (C1 and D0 steppings)
  - dwhciregister: 64-bit register addresses (uintptr; the Pi 4's are 32-bit values, unchanged)
  - lib/usb/gadget/Makefile: the gadget library on every RASPPI
  - dwusbgadget: the Pi 5 / CM5 accepted; on RASPPI 5 the core powered as Linux does ("set power state", device 3) and
    read whatever the firmware answers, any "OT2" core version, GHWCFG2-4 logged, the FIFO RAM checked; InitCorePi5's
    seven ways of bringing the core up from the firmware's host mode (usbinit=), Reconnect () to try another at run
    time, DumpRegisters (), GetUSBResetCount ()
  - dwusbgadget.cpp: the FIFOs as Linux sizes them for the dwc2 overlay: RX 558, NPTX 32, TX 512 x5, 256 x2 (this patch is
    applied in Pi 5 trees only)
  - dwusbgadgetendpoint.cpp: on RASPPI 5 DMA addresses are ARM physical addresses (/axi's dma-ranges map them 1:1),
    below 4 GB (asserted), not the VideoCore's 0xC0000000 alias
